      "text": "$$\\begin{align*}\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) &= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 - (2x^2 - x + 10x - 5)\\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 + x - 3 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{10x - 38}.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nGiven the above solution, write a Python script to determine the sum of the coefficients in $(X+13)(4X+1) - 4(2X^2+13X-2)$.\n\nPython script code:\n\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# define the variable X\nX = sp.symbols('X')\n\n# define the equation\nequation = (X + 13)*(4*X + 1) - 4*(2*X**2 + 13*X - 2)\n\n# extract the coefficients and find their sum\ncoeffs = sp.Poly(equation, X).all_coeffs()\nsum_of_coeffs = sum(coeffs)\n\nprint(sum_of_coeffs)",
